[38;5;231m⏺[39m Using hyperpowers:using-hyperpowers — the ladder puts this at rung 1, so I'm flagging the consequence before touching
  the file.

  The edit itself is one line: [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m → [38;5;153m480[39m in [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m ([38;5;153mserver.js:3[39m is the only consumer, and
  it reads the value directly, so nothing else changes).

  The consequence beyond that line: session lifetime is security posture. Going 30 minutes → 8 hours means a stolen or
  hijacked session token, or an unattended logged-in browser on a shared machine, stays valid for a full working day
  instead of half an hour — a 16x wider window. There's no idle-timeout or re-auth mechanism in this code to offset it.
